# Implementation Plan - Phase 3: AI & RAG Integration

## Goal Description
Integrate Artificial Intelligence capabilities into the backend. This includes setting up an LLM service (Google Gemini or OpenAI) for text generation and configuring a Vector Database (`pgvector`) to enable Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) for the tutoring system.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **LLM Provider**: Please specify if you prefer **Google Gemini** or **OpenAI**. I will assume **Google Gemini** for now as it offers a generous free tier.
> **API Key**: You will need to provide the API Key in the [.env](file:///d:/final%20year%20project/V/backend/.env) file (`GEMINI_API_KEY` or `OPENAI_API_KEY`).
> **PostgreSQL Extension**: Ensure your local PostgreSQL installation supports extensions. We will install the `vector` extension.

## Proposed Changes

### Dependencies
#### [MODIFY] [backend/requirements.txt](file:///d:/final year project/V/backend/requirements.txt)
- Add `google-generativeai` (for Gemini) or `openai`.
- Add `langchain`, `langchain-community` (for orchestration).
- Add `pgvector` (Python client) and `psycopg2-binary` (already there).
- Add `tiktoken` (for token counting).

### Database Setup
#### [NEW] [backend/rag/migrations/0001_enable_pgvector.py](file:///d:/final year project/V/backend/rag/migrations/0001_enable_pgvector.py)
- Create a migration to enable the `vector` extension in PostgreSQL: `CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector;`.

### RAG App Structure
#### [NEW] [backend/rag/](file:///d:/final year project/V/backend/rag/)
- Create a new Django app named `rag` to handle embeddings and retrieval.
- **Models**:
  - `KnowledgeChunk`: Store text content and its vector embedding.
    - Fields: `content` (TextField), `embedding` (VectorField), `source` (URL/Title).

### AI Service Layer
#### [NEW] [backend/rag/services.py](file:///d:/final year project/V/backend/rag/services.py)
- `LLMService`: Wrapper around the chosen LLM API.
  - `generate_response(prompt)`
- `EmbeddingService`: Wrapper to generate embeddings for text.
  - `embed_text(text)`

### API Endpoints
#### [NEW] [backend/rag/views.py](file:///d:/final year project/V/backend/rag/views.py)
- `AskAIView`: Endpoint where frontend sends a query, backend retrieves context, calls LLM, and returns answer.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Create a test script `test_rag.py` to:
  1.  Test connection to LLM API (simple "Hello" prompt).
  2.  Test embedding generation.
  3.  Test vector insertion and similarity search in DB.

### Manual Verification
- Use the `AskAIView` endpoint via Postman/cURL to ask a question and verify the response is relevant.
